// A type-returning FUNCTION head (`Make(i64)` where `Make :: ($T) -> Type`) is
// NON-transitive even when a DIRECT flat import authors the same name as an
// ORDINARY (non-type-returning) function. `main` flat-imports `b.sx`; `b.sx`
// declares `Make :: () -> i32` (a plain function, NOT a type-fn) AND flat-imports
// `c.sx`, whose `Make` IS the type-returning function. The only TYPE-FN author of
// `Make` is two flat hops away (main → b → c), so the bare `Make(i64)` head emits
// the "type 'Make' is not visible" diagnostic and poisons — the visible 1-hop
// ordinary `Make :: () -> i32` does NOT vouch for it.
//
// `headFnLeak`'s author view is narrowed to TYPE-FUNCTIONS (`typeFnAuthor`: a
// `fn_decl` with ≥1 `$`-param), the same discriminator every instantiation site
// uses to recognize a type-fn head, so an ordinary same-name function — which
// cannot be the head being instantiated — vouches for nothing.

#import "modules/std.sx";
#import "0771-modules-type-fn-head-ordinary-fn-no-vouch/b.sx";

main :: () -> i32 {
    print("size={}\n", size_of(Make(i64)));
    0
}
